watch-offline-probe — the 2026-10-20 tick: the interface had no address when the
tunnel was about to be probed (rowt #s57).

Built on watch-no-exit: the router is up (host.pid.self), the system proxy
points at it, and bind_interface is en0. ROWT_IFACE=en0 on the case line names
the interface without checking it, the way a real tick can read the interface a
moment before its address goes. `ipconfig getifaddr en0` answers nothing (exit
1), so the network id is "ParityNet none/192.0.2.1"; watch.net already holds it,
so phase two reaches the health check instead of logging a move. watch.health
seeds a streak of one.

Expected: the shell's `_watch_health` returns before its probe, resets the
streak and records `result=offline` in watch.last, logging nothing; the planner
must agree. Before probe_offline existed the shadow told it `health_ok: false`,
and it planned "escape tunnel probe failed (2/3)".
